DESIGN GOAL:

With this new objective added to the game, I wanted my army to really focus on capturing and securing the objective. I made the footman group up much quicker and push the zone, acting as the wall while the
archers and cavalry played more offensive roles.

REFLECTION:

I finally used the chat function in this season. I ran into a lot of issues where my troops lacked the information to fulfill their role to the fullest; for example, not seeing an enemy that an ally sees.
Adding the chat function improved the cooperation of the army by making them talk to each other.
I also used the lookAhead function to improve cavalry efficiency. I wanted my cavalry to prioritize targeting archers, but that sometimes meant they would waste turns not doing the optimal play. For example,
if the archer was too far, the cavalry would not attack anything that turn. Using lookAhead allowed me to make sure that cavalry troops were more efficient.

AI DISCLOSURE:

I used Claude Code extensively in this assignment. Claude helped me modify and improve my code. I checked its work by rereading its changes and watching the agent with every modification.
Using this coding agent definitely made the assignment easier and coding it was faster.
